<!--
  CAP 1.2 rendering of examples/01-structure-fire.json, per GFN v0.1 Section 11.3.

  Two things to note:

  1. The area/polygon coordinate order is "latitude,longitude", which is the
     REVERSE of the GeoJSON "[longitude, latitude]" order in the source notice.
     This is the most common integration defect in geospatial alerting.

  2. The complete signed GFN notice travels in the GFN-payload parameter. A
     receiver MUST decode and verify that payload and treat it as authoritative.
     The CAP elements below are a lossy, human-readable rendering.

  3. No EAS-ORG parameter appears here. The source notice's channels are
     DIRECT_API and IPAWS, not EAS, and Section 11.4 is explicit that a routine
     geofence notice does not belong on the public alerting channels.
-->
